2006; 24:341–8.</cite> [<a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.immuni.2006.02.006" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DOI</a>] [<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16546102/" class="usa-link">PubMed</a>] [<a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?journal=Immunity&amp;title=Cytokine%20milieu%20of%20atopic%20dermatitis%20skin%20subverts%20the%20innate%20immune%20response%20to%20vaccinia%20virus&amp;author=MD%20Howell&amp;author=RL%20Gallo&amp;author=M%20Boguniewicz&amp;volume=24&amp;publication_year=2006&amp;pages=341-8&amp;pmid=16546102&amp;doi=10.1016/j.immuni.2006.02.006&amp;" class="usa-link usa-link--external" data-ga-action="click_feat_suppl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar</a>]</li>
</ul></section></section><section id="_ad93_" lang="en" class="associated-data"><h2 class="pmc_sec_title">Associated Data</h2>
<p class="font-secondary"><em>This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article.</em></p>
<section id="_adsm93_" lang="en" class="supplementary-materials"><h3 class="pmc_sec_title">Supplementary Materials</h3>
<section class="sm xbox font-sm" id="db_ds_supplementary-material1_reqid_"><div class="caption p">
<p>
<strong>Appendix S1</strong> Study investigators.</p>
<p>
<strong>Appendix S2</strong> Additional study methods.</p>
<p>
<strong>Figure S1</strong> Trial design.</p>
<p>
<strong>Figure S2</strong> Testing hierarchy.</p>
<p>
<strong>Figure S3</strong> Patient disposition.</p>
<p>
<strong>Figure S4</strong> Initiation of rescue medication and permanent discontinuation of the investigational medicinal product, initial treatment period.</p>
<p>
<strong>Figure S5</strong> Change from baseline in (a) SCORing Atopic Dermatitis, (b) weekly average of worst daily pruritus numerical rating scale (NRS), (c) Dermatology Life Quality Index and (d) eczema‐related sleep interference NRS throughout the initial treatment period in ECZTRA 1 and ECZTRA 2.</p>
<p>
<strong>Figure S6</strong> (a) Eczema Area and Severity Index ≥ 50% and (b) Eczema Area and Severity Index ≥ 90% response rates in the initial treatment period in ECZTRA 1 and ECZTRA 2.</p>
<p>
<strong>Figure S7</strong> Percentage change from baseline in Eczema Area and Severity Index throughout the initial treatment period.</p>
<p>
<strong>Table S1</strong> Previous atopic dermatitis treatments, randomized patients.</p>
<p>
<strong>Table S2</strong> Rescue medication use by type during the initial treatment period, randomized patients.</p>
<p>
<strong>Table S3</strong> Investigator’s Global Assessment 0 or 1 by visit, initial treatment period, observed cases: full analysis set.</p>
<p>
<strong>Table S4</strong> Change from baseline in Eczema Area and Severity Index by visit, initial treatment period, observed cases: full analysis set.</p>
<p>
<strong>Table S5</strong> Primary efficacy outcomes assessed using the primary and alternative estimand approaches.</p>
<p>
<strong>Table S6</strong> SCORing Atopic Dermatitis by visit, initial treatment period, observed cases: full analysis set.</p>
<p>
<strong>Table S7</strong> Change from baseline in SCORing Atopic Dermatitis by visit, repeated‐measurements analysis, initial treatment period: full analysis set.</p>
<p>
<strong>Table S8</strong> Dermatology Life Quality Index by visit, initial treatment period, observed cases: full analysis set.</p>
<p>
<strong>Table S9</strong> Change from baseline in Dermatology Life Quality Index by visit, repeated‐measurements analysis, initial treatment period: full analysis set.</p>
<p>
<strong>Table S10</strong> Reduction in weekly average of worst daily pruritus numerical rating scale ≥ 4 at week 16 in the initial treatment period, all analyses: full analysis set.</p>
<p>
<strong>Table S11</strong> Change from baseline in SCORing Atopic Dermatitis and Dermatology Life Quality Index at week 16 in the initial treatment period, all analyses: full analysis set.</p>
<p>
<strong>Table S12</strong> Adverse events in the 36‐week maintenance treatment period in patients who received tralokinumab in the initial treatment period.</p>
</div>
